"Did you create these words with a passphrase?" = "你创建这些单词时用了密码短语吗?";
"A passphrase is an extra word or sentence you add on top of your 12 or 24 words. It is optional, and most people do not use one." = "密码短语是在你的 12 或 24 个单词之外额外加上的一个词或一句话。它是可选的，大多数人都不用。";
"It does not lock your account" = "它不会给你的账户上锁";
"This is the part people get wrong. A passphrase does not put a password on your account. It opens a completely different account. Your 12 or 24 words with no passphrase open one account. The same words with the word \"apple\" opens another one. With \"banana\", another one again. Every passphrase is its own separate account, with its own address and its own balance." = "这是大家最容易搞错的地方。密码短语并不是给你的账户加密码。它会打开一个完全不同的账户。不带密码短语的 12 或 24 个单词打开一个账户。同样的单词加上 \"apple\" 会打开另一个账户。加上 \"banana\"，又是另一个。每个密码短语都是一个独立的账户，有自己的地址和余额。";
"Why anyone bothers" = "为什么有人要用";
"If someone finds your written 12 or 24 words, they get the account those words open on their own. They do not get the one behind your passphrase, because they do not know there is one, and they could not guess it anyway." = "如果有人找到你写下的 12 或 24 个单词，他只能拿到这些单词单独打开的那个账户。他拿不到你密码短语背后的账户，因为他不知道有密码短语，而且也猜不出来。";
"The catch" = "代价";
"There is no reset and no recovery. If you forget your passphrase, the account it opened is gone for good. Your 12 or 24 words alone will not bring it back, and nobody can help you. Treat it exactly like the words themselves: written down, somewhere safe, before you rely on it." = "无法重置，也无法找回。如果你忘了密码短语，它打开的账户就永远丢失了。仅凭 12 或 24 个单词无法找回，也没有人能帮你。请像对待单词本身一样对待它：在依赖它之前，先写下来并放在安全的地方。";
"One more thing to know" = "还有一点要知道";
"If you type the wrong passphrase, nothing will tell you. You will simply land in a different account, and it will look empty. That is not a bug and your money is not lost - it just means you are in the wrong account." = "如果你输错了密码短语，不会有任何提示。你只是进入了另一个账户，而它看起来是空的。这不是故障，你的钱也没有丢 - 只是说明你进错了账户。";
"So do you need one?" = "那你需要吗?";
"If you are not sure, you do not need one: go back to the start and tap Create New Account, which makes an account without a passphrase. It is still protected by your 12 or 24 words, and you can always create another account with a passphrase later." = "如果你不确定，那就不需要：回到开头并轻点「创建新账户」，它会创建一个不带密码短语的账户。它仍受你的 12 或 24 个单词保护，以后你也随时可以再创建一个带密码短语的账户。";
"If you never set one up, choose No. A passphrase is something you would have typed in on purpose, so if this is the first you are hearing of it, you do not have one." = "如果你从未设置过，请选择「否」。密码短语是你会特意输入的东西，所以如果你是第一次听说，那你就没有。";
"Hashrate is how much computing power miners are pointing at Kaspa. A higher hashrate means more work securing the chain, and it moves with mining profitability rather than with the price directly. Figures come from the Kaspa REST API set in Connection Settings, at one sample per day." = "算力是矿工投向 Kaspa 的计算能力。算力越高，保护链的工作就越多；它随挖矿收益变化，而不是直接随价格变化。数据来自连接设置中指定的 Kaspa REST API，每天一个样本。";
"Automatic scan enabled." = "已开启自动扫描。";
"Node updated." = "节点已更新。";
"Import failed." = "导入失败。";
